    "description": "- Responsible for completely rewriting a legacy VB6 application using current C# and WPF technologies. The application is in a staged roll-out.\n- Responsible for creating a simple MVVM framework for use in-house (as an alternative to using Prism or MVVMLight).\n- Responsible for creating a UI framework with the goal of enforcing some style guidelines. \n- The UI framework both gives a nice modern style to all apps, but also forces them to look alike and give cohesion to our suite of internal applications.\n- The framework also has a number of built in features to speed up development in WPF. These include modal dialog helpers and dynamically build settings controls.\n- Created an internal tool built on top of click once (the company’s preferred deployment tool) to simplify deployment to multiple plants with different deployment parameters (connection strings etc.)\n- Responsible for creating a shape viewing component. This allows all company applications to use a shared drawing component for displaying our windows and their varying shapes. This is built in WPF as a custom control. \n",
